    "created_at": "2016-05-03T08:25:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-03T08:25:52Z",
    "body": "I'm thinking whether `<a href=x rel=alternate type=application/atom+xml>` should be non-conforming, but figure it could be used as a styling hook. Looking at https://github.com/search?utf8=✓&q=\"rel+alternate+type+application\"+NOT+link&type=Code&ref=searchresults it seems there is some usage without a `link` element. Maybe conformance checkers should give a warning if they find an `a`/`area` element but have not seen a `link` element for a feed? cc @sideshowbarker \n",
